1
00:00:00,801 --> 00:00:03,323
So let's show a confirmation modal here.

2
00:00:04,364 --> 00:00:06,801
And for that, I'll create a new constant

3
00:00:06,801 --> 00:00:06,930
here,

4
00:00:07,464 --> 00:00:10,440
confirmationModal,

5
00:00:12,461 --> 00:00:14,531
and I'll store a string in there. I'll store

6
00:00:14,564 --> 00:00:16,957
the HTML code in there that should be shown

7
00:00:17,006 --> 00:00:17,491
on the screen.

8
00:00:18,542 --> 00:00:21,760
And I actually prepared that markup for you.

9
00:00:22,099 --> 00:00:24,250
You find it attached so that you can just

10
00:00:24,347 --> 00:00:26,740
paste it into your string here. So that's

11
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:28,669
the markup you find attached to this

12
00:00:28,767 --> 00:00:29,061
lecture.

13
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:33,783
This will render a dialog with a class of

14
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:37,060
modal, with some text and with 2 buttons,

15
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:40,045
one for confirming the submission and one

16
00:00:40,158 --> 00:00:41,223
for canceling it.

17
00:00:42,901 --> 00:00:45,111
Now, adding this constant here, of course,

18
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:47,790
won't achieve anything. Instead, we'll need

19
00:00:47,822 --> 00:00:50,467
to make sure that this confirmation modal is

20
00:00:50,587 --> 00:00:51,584
rendered onto the screen.

21
00:00:52,935 --> 00:00:54,770
And we can achieve this by reaching out to

22
00:00:54,770 --> 00:00:55,607
our document

23
00:00:56,154 --> 00:00:57,571
and then there the body element.

24
00:00:58,328 --> 00:00:59,745
And on that body we can call

25
00:00:59,922 --> 00:01:00,517
insertAdjacentHTML,

26
00:01:03,512 --> 00:01:05,874
which allows us to insert some HTML into the

27
00:01:05,922 --> 00:01:06,211
body.

28
00:01:06,789 --> 00:01:08,862
And this specific method allows us to

29
00:01:08,878 --> 00:01:10,597
control where we wanna add it.

30
00:01:11,368 --> 00:01:13,489
Here I wanna add it to the end or at the end

31
00:01:13,489 --> 00:01:14,004
of the body.

32
00:01:15,083 --> 00:01:17,353
And then the HTML I wanna add is of course

33
00:01:17,643 --> 00:01:20,202
this HTML markup, which is stored in this

34
00:01:20,315 --> 00:01:21,329
confirmation modal.

35
00:01:24,272 --> 00:01:26,719
Constant. So that should add the dialog on

36
00:01:26,752 --> 00:01:27,218
the screen,

37
00:01:28,054 --> 00:01:30,995
but this dialog element actually works such

38
00:01:31,108 --> 00:01:33,949
that by default it's invisible. The dialog

39
00:01:33,949 --> 00:01:35,544
is not open by default.

40
00:01:37,017 --> 00:01:39,508
Therefore, what we have to do here is

41
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:43,003
open the dialog manually after it has been

42
00:01:43,003 --> 00:01:43,439
inserted.

43
00:01:44,718 --> 00:01:48,271
So I'll select that inserted dialog by using

44
00:01:48,448 --> 00:01:51,751
document.querySelector and selecting the

45
00:01:51,751 --> 00:01:54,686
first, and in this case, only dialog element

46
00:01:54,686 --> 00:01:57,364
I'll find on the page, which is the dialog

47
00:01:57,364 --> 00:01:59,016
that was inserted by this line of code.

48
00:02:00,330 --> 00:02:02,143
And then we can use that underlying

49
00:02:02,255 --> 00:02:05,767
JavaScript object that is made available by

50
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:08,525
querySelector for this dialog DOM element.

51
00:02:09,776 --> 00:02:12,486
We can use that to call showModal, which is

52
00:02:12,582 --> 00:02:15,638
a built-in method. Provided by the browser

53
00:02:15,879 --> 00:02:18,040
for this dialog HTML element.

54
00:02:18,717 --> 00:02:20,973
And that will then actually open it and show

55
00:02:20,973 --> 00:02:21,618
it on the screen.

56
00:02:23,762 --> 00:02:26,382
So that will show us this modal, but we'll

57
00:02:26,398 --> 00:02:27,191
have a problem.

58
00:02:27,951 --> 00:02:28,032
The

59
00:02:28,824 --> 00:02:32,447
HTTP request which HTMX wants to send

60
00:02:33,045 --> 00:02:36,328
will still be sent no matter if we show this

61
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,217
dialog or not.

62
00:02:38,122 --> 00:02:41,114
And of course, I don't wanna send it just

63
00:02:41,114 --> 00:02:43,420
yet. I wanna send it later once we know that

64
00:02:43,436 --> 00:02:46,879
the user confirmed the submission with this

65
00:02:46,976 --> 00:02:48,964
Yes button and I don't wanna send it at all

66
00:02:49,158 --> 00:02:50,678
if the user clicked the No button.

67
00:02:52,486 --> 00:02:54,475
And therefore what we can do here

68
00:02:55,074 --> 00:02:57,080
is accept an event argument

69
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:59,732
which will be passed into this function

70
00:03:00,201 --> 00:03:02,254
since it's defined as the event handling

71
00:03:02,351 --> 00:03:04,627
function down there automatically by the

72
00:03:04,627 --> 00:03:05,111
browser.

73
00:03:06,548 --> 00:03:09,760
And the event object we'll receive here will

74
00:03:09,873 --> 00:03:12,706
be an event object that has a preventDefault

75
00:03:12,706 --> 00:03:15,244
method default method, which in the end

76
00:03:15,277 --> 00:03:18,449
cancels the event, which then in turn will

77
00:03:18,513 --> 00:03:22,104
make sure that HTMX will not proceed and

78
00:03:22,185 --> 00:03:23,926
will not send that request.

79
00:03:25,678 --> 00:03:29,447
I'll also console.log this event object so

80
00:03:29,447 --> 00:03:31,437
that we can see what else is in there,

81
00:03:32,214 --> 00:03:34,365
which kind of information might be attached

82
00:03:34,494 --> 00:03:35,013
to this event.

83
00:03:36,426 --> 00:03:38,488
Because in the end, we're handling a custom

84
00:03:38,618 --> 00:03:41,671
event created by HTMX and it's definitely

85
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,036
interesting to see which extra metadata

86
00:03:44,842 --> 00:03:47,781
information is attached to that event object

87
00:03:48,215 --> 00:03:50,672
by HTMX. That's why I'm logging it here.

88
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:54,897
But with this code, we're now canceling the

89
00:03:54,897 --> 00:03:57,097
event. We're making sure that the request is

90
00:03:57,226 --> 00:03:59,218
not getting sent. We're looking into the

91
00:03:59,218 --> 00:04:02,189
event and we're showing that dialog.

92
00:04:03,474 --> 00:04:06,285
So if you save everything and you reload,

93
00:04:07,313 --> 00:04:08,743
if you click on one of these items,

94
00:04:09,642 --> 00:04:11,982
you should see that it's not added here to

95
00:04:11,982 --> 00:04:12,727
the list at the top,

96
00:04:13,455 --> 00:04:15,088
that instead we have this dialog

97
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:17,806
where we need to replace this placeholder

98
00:04:18,065 --> 00:04:19,891
with more useful text in the future

99
00:04:20,712 --> 00:04:22,545
and where those buttons don't do anything

100
00:04:22,577 --> 00:04:22,819
yet,

101
00:04:23,703 --> 00:04:26,679
but where we also have this custom event

102
00:04:26,679 --> 00:04:28,417
here in our developer tools.

103
00:04:30,402 --> 00:04:33,528
And this event object has some default

104
00:04:33,608 --> 00:04:36,089
properties which all JavaScript events have.

105
00:04:36,927 --> 00:04:39,784
But we also have a detail property there

106
00:04:39,897 --> 00:04:42,481
which holds an object with some extra data

107
00:04:42,561 --> 00:04:44,487
that is added by HTMX.

108
00:04:45,755 --> 00:04:47,617
And here, for example, in that detail

109
00:04:47,617 --> 00:04:49,912
property on that event object, we have an

110
00:04:50,249 --> 00:04:53,604
elt property which gives us access to the

111
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:56,685
element that triggered the event in case we

112
00:04:56,685 --> 00:04:57,552
might need that.

113
00:04:58,274 --> 00:05:00,634
For this specific event, which is about

114
00:05:00,634 --> 00:05:03,362
sending an HTTP request, we, for example,

115
00:05:03,491 --> 00:05:06,730
also get the configured XMLHttpRequest

116
00:05:06,858 --> 00:05:09,839
object as a property in the event data.

117
00:05:11,201 --> 00:05:13,572
And you can use all that event data in

118
00:05:13,829 --> 00:05:16,281
whatever way you need to use it for your

119
00:05:16,409 --> 00:05:17,018
application.

120
00:05:18,316 --> 00:05:20,463
And indeed, in the next lecture, we're going

121
00:05:20,479 --> 00:05:23,700
to use this detail object to improve the

122
00:05:23,764 --> 00:05:26,488
text in this dialog before we then of course

123
00:05:26,568 --> 00:05:28,811
also make sure that these buttons work and

124
00:05:28,892 --> 00:05:29,420
do something.
